<article class="env-example" id="0074">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0074">Example <span data-tag="0074">6.9.3</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a topological space. For each open $U \subset X$ consider the $\mathbf{R}$-algebra $\mathcal{C}^{0}(U) = \{  f : U \to \mathbf{R} \mid f\text{ is continuous}\} $. There are obvious restriction mappings that turn this into a presheaf of $\mathbf{R}$-algebras over $X$. By Example <a href="/tag/006V" data-tag="006V">6.7.3</a> it is a sheaf of sets. Hence by the Lemma <a href="/tag/0073" data-tag="0073">6.9.2</a> it is a sheaf of $\mathbf{R}$-algebras over $X$. </p>
</article>